<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65930" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελάν-ω</span></b> , intr., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>grow black</i>, only in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				7.64
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεφύροιο ἐχεύατο πόντον ἔπι φρίξ . . ,
				μελάνει δέ τε πόντος ὑπ᾽ αὐτῆς</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς φρικός</span>), cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				934a15
			</span></i>; but <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> read <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόντον</span> in the second
			clause and took <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελάνει</span> trans., 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελαίνει</span>
			 (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζέφυρος</span>),
			<i>makes</i> the sea <i>black</i>:—later writers use
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελανέω</span></b> , intr. (which
			implies the reading <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μελανεῖ δέ τε
			πόντος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Ign.</u>
				50
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.1574
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				836
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ καλὸν μελανεῦντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Epigr.</u>
					53
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μικκὴ καὶ μελανεῦσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					5.120
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
